{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The IvorGeneralMIDI framework provides the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/midi.org\/general-midi"},{"type":"text","text":" and General MIDI 2 sound sets as Swift"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"enumerations. For General MIDI 1: the 128 instruments that a program change"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"selects, the 16 instrument families they fall into, and the 47 sounds of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"percussion key map. For General MIDI 2: the 256 instruments that a bank select"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and program change select, the 9 drum sets, and the 61 sounds of the extended"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"percussion key map. Each sound can be looked up by its program, bank, or note,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or by its name as the specification gives it, and converted back again."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Programs, notes, and channels use the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/eBardX\/IvorMIDI"},{"type":"text","text":" data value types, and the system"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exclusive messages that turn General MIDI on and off are available as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"MIDISystemMessage","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" values."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import IvorGeneralMIDI","","let guitar = GM1Instrument(program: 25)","","guitar              \/\/ .acousticGuitarNylon","guitar.name         \/\/ \"Acoustic Guitar (nylon)\"","guitar.family       \/\/ .guitar","","\/\/ Name lookup ignores case and extra whitespace.","let snare = GM1PercussionSound(name: \"acoustic snare\")","","snare?.note         \/\/ 38","GM1PercussionSound.channel  \/\/ 10","","\/\/ A General MIDI 2 variation falls back to its General MIDI 1 instrument.","let ukulele = GM2Instrument(bankLSB: 1, program: 25)","","ukulele?.name           \/\/ \"Ukulele\"","ukulele?.gm1Instrument  \/\/ .acousticGuitarNylon","GM2Instrument.bankMSB   \/\/ 121","","\/\/ Bank select MSB 121, bank select LSB 1, then program change 25.","let messages = ukulele?.selectionMessages(channel: 1)","","MIDISystemMessage.gm2SystemOn  \/\/ F0 7E 7F 09 03 F7"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/documentation\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/UsingIvorGeneralMIDI"},{"type":"text","text":" for a full guide to the instruments, drum sets,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"percussion sounds, and General MIDI 2 effects and controllers."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/documentation\/IvorGeneralMIDI"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"General MIDI 1 and 2 instrument, drum set, and percussion sound types.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"role":"collection","color":{"standardColorIdentifier":"blue"},"roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"IvorGeneralMIDI"}],"externalID":"IvorGeneralMIDI","symbolKind":"module","title":"IvorGeneralMIDI"},"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"title":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/documentation\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/UsingIvorGeneralMIDI"],"anchor":"Guides"},{"title":"General MIDI 1","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/documentation\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/GM1Instrument","doc:\/\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/documentation\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/GM1InstrumentFamily","doc:\/\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/documentation\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/GM1PercussionSound"],"anchor":"General-MIDI-1"},{"title":"General MIDI 2","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/documentation\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/GM2